WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:04.759
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and so much went
down on Arrow this week that I’m going to

00:00:04.759 --> 00:00:07.980
add a few bonus moments to my top 5 list.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.160
But we have a lot we need to talk about.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.740
And in case you didn’t know there are only
three more episode left this season.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:17.960
I was going to post a bonus video this morning
but I had some technical issues and now I’m

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.250
just posting it in a few hours.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.009
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:00:22.009 --> 00:00:27.390
I’ll also have a link to it in the description.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:30.789
So careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode yet, but let’s start with top

00:00:30.789 --> 00:00:31.789
5 moments.

00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:34.650
Number 5 - Roy Flips His Shit On Everyone

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.850
Did anyone else get a Frankenstein vibe with
him lying there on the table?

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:41.340
They could have done this episode during Halloween
and it would have been appropriate.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:46.840
I knew that he’d hallucinate Thea, but I
was surprised that she told him to kill her.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:51.710
Slade’s Shado hallucination seems a little
more insidious, but I guess it just depends

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:54.540
on what your mind is like before you get injected
with mirakuru.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.040
In case you don’t remember back to Heir
to the Demon, episode 13, they’ve got him

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.460
on an IV Drip of the Pit Viper Venom Nyssa
Al Ghul was using.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.220
It’s supposed to be enough to take down
an elephant.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:05.249
So until the cure is ready, they’re going
to keep Roy in a medically induced coma.

00:01:05.249 --> 00:01:09.560
In real life that’s really common for patients
who are at risk for injuring themselves really

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.000
badly.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.420
My big surprise in all this was mostly that
Sin seems to not be in on any of the Team

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:17.840
Arrow stuff.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:22.600
I thought she was like Sara’s partner in
crime, but I guess she’s more like a sister,

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:23.600
like Laurel.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:27.149
Number 4 - Sara Breaks Up With Oliver and
Takes Off

00:01:27.149 --> 00:01:30.069
Biggest question was who is that old friend.

00:01:30.069 --> 00:01:33.880
My first guess is that it’s Slade, but I
think based on what happened later in the

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:36.479
episode, she’s going back to the League
of Assassin’s.

00:01:36.479 --> 00:01:41.420
I’m expecting them to come back to Starling
City before the finale and run clean up on

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.549
some of Slade’s mirakuru soldiers.

00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:45.939
So maybe that’s what Sara’s comeback moment
will be.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.860
She’ll come back in the darkest hour.

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:53.500
I got really worried when she started all
that darkness inside me talk, as if the writers

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.510
were laying groundwork for her eventual death.

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:02.039
But there had been so many other clues that
she’d live, especially all the Birds of

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:03.759
Prey talk.

00:02:03.759 --> 00:02:07.069
It took the rest of the episode to figure
it all out.

00:02:07.069 --> 00:02:11.120
High Fives to the writers for pulling a bit
of a misdirect with that last big scene.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:15.510
Right now we only have episode descriptions
up to the finale.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:18.730
So it doesn’t look like Sara will be back
until Episode 23.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:21.349
Hopefully she’ll bring Ra’s Al Ghul with
her.

00:02:21.349 --> 00:02:24.060
Number 3 - Oliver Is Out Of Commission

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:27.599
His leg is pretty f’d up which is why he
pretty much jumped into Felicity’s arms

00:02:27.599 --> 00:02:28.660
at the bottom of the stairs.

00:02:28.660 --> 00:02:32.680
Who else got a flashback to last season when
he carried her in his arms.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:36.209
It was a nice funny moment in an otherwise
shocking episode.

00:02:36.209 --> 00:02:37.770
Felicity as always had the best jokes in the
episode.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:39.930
Can you even fit into those leather pants?

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:42.900
And she made fun of him for being too heavy.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:46.689
Who else laughed out loud when Oliver was
like where are the drugs, I need all of the

00:02:46.689 --> 00:02:47.689
drugs.

00:02:47.689 --> 00:02:48.800
And just downed everything.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:55.120
I think it was barely enough to keep him standing
without crying while they subdued Roy.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:03:01.770
I kept getting the feeling that the writers
wanted us to wonder whether or not Oliver

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:03.290
would take the Mirakuru.

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:06.239
He can’t, they can’t synthesize anymore,
and the last sample is being used by Caitlin

00:03:06.239 --> 00:03:12.310
Snow to make the cure at Star Labs in Central
City.

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:16.260
Number 2 - Oliver has a Child

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:19.560
I didn’t see the name of that woman, so
if they wrote it in the credits please add

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:20.940
it in the comments below.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:26.659
But we should assume his child is still alive
and in Central City.

00:03:26.659 --> 00:03:30.270
They were fuzzy on how far back that flashback
went, but I’d guess the boy or girl would

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.829
be between 6 and 7 years old.

00:03:32.829 --> 00:03:37.659
Old enough for a young actor to be cast with
speaking lines.

00:03:37.659 --> 00:03:41.000
Remember Slade said that one other person
had to die.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:46.810
I think that in the finale “Unthinkable”
Slade will magic up Oliver’s child and threaten

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:47.870
their life.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:52.770
I’m avoiding pronouns, but I think we’re
all expecting a Connor Hawke situation.

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:57.250
That’s such a huge place for the story to
go in season 3, I totally think that said

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:01.890
child will survive and be a part of what happens
going forward.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:06.180
Him living in Central City is just another
perfect opportunity to link Arrow and Flash

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.180
stories.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:11.049
Now Oliver has a reason to quote unquote visit
Barry’s city.

00:04:11.049 --> 00:04:12.069
Let me know if you agree.

00:04:12.069 --> 00:04:15.999
and my Number 1 moment - Slade kills Moira
Queen

00:04:15.999 --> 00:04:20.459
Huge WTF, but there were some parts of this
that I expected and a few things about it

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:22.190
that really surprised me.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:28.190
First, in my finale predictions video I did
last week, I predicted Moira would die.

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:30.060
But I didn’t think she would die this way.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:36.270
I expected Slade to use Felicity, Sara and
Felicity, or Thea or really any of the other

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:40.479
women except for Moira.

00:04:40.479 --> 00:04:46.169
Remember, she never told Oliver about his
son and she didn’t have time to tell them

00:04:46.169 --> 00:04:47.699
Merlyn is still alive.

00:04:47.699 --> 00:04:51.259
So they have a few surprises in store.

00:04:51.259 --> 00:04:55.360
I think they did a really good job of sending
the character off, they gave her that very

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:58.900
dignified moment at the end where she chose
her children over her own life.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:02.349
And Slade even called her out on it and gave
her respect.

00:05:02.349 --> 00:05:06.590
I think that’s why he used the blade instead
of shooting her in the head.

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:09.639
I really love that she and Oliver had that
other moment earlier where she let him know

00:05:09.639 --> 00:05:12.730
she knew about the Arrow and they reconciled.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:18.720
So before we talk about repercussions from
all this let me know what your favorite moment

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.680
was.

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:24.770
The Connor Hawke teaser, Moira dying or something
else?

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:28.460
The thing that’s really sticking with me
right now is Slade’s line, “There’s

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:30.759
still one more person that has to die.”

00:05:30.759 --> 00:05:34.690
So let’s talk about what all this means
for the final episodes.

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:39.940
First off, next week we saw in the teaser:
The funeral, Oliver can’t be found, Slade

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:48.360
unleashes his army, including Ravager and
Brother Blood has his big moment.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:52.770
So things are going to get worse before they
get better, but like I said.

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:57.319
I expect Oliver’s Child to be a plot point
before the end of the season, Sara will be

00:05:57.319 --> 00:06:01.050
back with the League of Assassins and Merlyn
is also coming back.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:03.720
We’re not really sure what he’s going
to do.

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:12.379
He could either just take Thea away or help
them out.

00:06:12.379 --> 00:06:16.889
Overall I gave the episode a solid A. They
keep making things worse and worse for Oliver

00:06:16.889 --> 00:06:21.580
and Team Arrow and it’s only going to make
their victory that much sweeter.

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:25.430
More than any other show this year with the
exception of Game of Thrones, I think Arrow

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:28.879
has surprised me the most with how much fun
it’s been to analyze week to week.

00:06:28.879 --> 00:06:33.440
It’s a big tribute to the writers that what
they and the cast and crew have done lends

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:35.590
itself to heavy analysis and discussion.

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:47.889
The only thing I’m still waiting for is
Thea to either pick up a bow and head down

00:06:47.889 --> 00:06:51.889
Oliver’s path or follow Laurel and become
just a more self-actualized stealth member

00:06:51.889 --> 00:06:52.940
of the team.

00:06:52.940 --> 00:06:56.569
I was happy to see Sin again, I think she’ll
be around for the finale.

00:06:56.569 --> 00:07:01.560
I’m hoping she and Roy get to have some
more Young Justice moments next season where

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:03.300
they go off on missions by themselves.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:07.449
That’s another thing I’ll talk about more
when the finale is over.

00:07:07.449 --> 00:07:10.370
Them doing more odd pairings of characters
in season 3.

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:13.900
Like for instance, Diggle and Thea had a scene
together and we haven’t really seen them

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:16.050
get a moment like that in a long long time.

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:17.449
It was really good.

00:07:17.449 --> 00:07:21.280
Let me know in the comments which characters
you want to see have scenes together that

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:23.120
normally wouldn't’t.

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:28.569
Like Quentyn and Diggle at a bar telling stories.

00:07:28.569 --> 00:07:32.550
Like I said, I’ll post that bonus video
in a couple hours.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:37.050
It’s my Top 10 Team Arrow moments this season.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:38.050
Moments when it’s just the team.

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:39.050
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:40.050
And leave me suggestions for future bonus
videos.

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:41.050
Right now you can click here for that video.

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:43.220
I’ll update the link as soon as I post it.

00:07:43.220 --> 00:07:45.680
And you can click here for my Q&amp;A video.

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:47.710
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:48.410
High Fives!

